00:05:09.795 --> 00:05:11.631
(instructor speaking in foreign language)

00:05:11.631 --> 00:05:13.440
And now let's take a look at the solution.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.990
So there might be a number of ways

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.200
to solve it but the simplest way I found

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:22.840
was to try and find out
how many TVs each degree

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.040
of the pie represents.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.760
I'm going to define this variable X,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.070
which is how many TVs there are

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:33.360
in each degree of the pie in 2019.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.720
And also, I'm going to define why,

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.270
which is the same thing

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.650
but for the 2020 pie chart.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:40.810
Now let's look at the chart.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.660
We will want to know how many degrees

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:45.720
are in this section K.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.270
At first glance, it might
look like it's 1/3, 120,

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:52.010
like this one down here
but actually, it's not.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:57.010
If this one here, L, is
90 degrees, M is 120,

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.230
and in total, this has to add to 360,

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.100
then K will actually be 150 degrees.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.610
Over here it's a bit more simple.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:10.010
We've got 90, 90 and so this
one would have to be 180.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.340
If we can find x,

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:12.900
then the problem will be solved

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.943
by finding 150 times x.

00:06:15.943 --> 00:06:19.470
That will be how many TVs
this chunk represents.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.212
If that's 150x,

00:06:21.212 --> 00:06:26.212
then this one here is 90x, 120x.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.970
Since the number of M
brand televisions increases

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.830
in number by 40,

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:36.830
then this section here
will be 120x plus 40.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.620
And since L decreases in number by 25,

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:46.507
this one here will be 90x minus 25.

00:06:46.507 --> 00:06:50.170
And these segments can also
be represented using y.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:54.880
This one is also 90 degrees times y

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.670
and this one down here is 180y.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:00.040
And since these represent the same number

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.830
of TVs in this chunk,

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.560
we can write 90x minus 25

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:05.913
is equal to 90y.

00:07:06.924 --> 00:07:07.930
And for this one,

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:12.930
120x plus 40 is equal to 180y.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.940
This is our key to solving the problem.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.940
We've got two unknowns

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.520
but also two equations,

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:22.520
so we can solve this for both x and y.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.280
Rearranging the top one for y

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.350
and subbing that into the second one,

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.670
I get x to be 3/2.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:32.330
Remember what we wanted to
solve the problem was 150x.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:36.460
So 150 times 3/2.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.757
Well, that is 450/2,

00:07:39.757 --> 00:07:41.187
which is equal to 225,

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.770
meaning that C is the correct answer.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:48.080
Now, it took me a few goes to get there

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.230
but if you found this
easily, then congratulations,

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:54.130
you're as smart as a Turkish 13-year-old.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:55.170
I can't help but think

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:57.540
that if you already are studying so hard

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.090
for exams this early

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:00.350
that by the time you get

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.010
to those tougher
university entrance exams,

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:04.880
you may have already burned out.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.950
But it seems like even getting into some

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:10.300
of the best high schools
is a competitive process.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.210
This is a question

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:14.320
from that notorious
university entrance exam.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:19.080
This is from the 2021
AYT mathematics paper.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.610
Translated, it says that P of x

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:23.410
is a fourth degree polynomial

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.430
with real coefficients.

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:27.820
And it gives the inequality that P of x

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.010
is bigger than or equal to x.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:32.500
It gives us three values of P of x

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.860
at x is one, two and three.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.360
And it asks us to find the value of P of x

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.370
at x is equal to four.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.430
Now, on an axes of x and P of x,

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:45.400
this line here represents

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.760
where P of x is equal to x.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.390
Our function is called P of x

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:52.450
but it could just as
easily have been called y

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:53.890
and you may recognize this

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.210
as more commonly called
the line y equals x.

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:59.010
This inequality tells us

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.920
that the value of our function

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:04.710
will always exist above or at this line.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.850
So in this region here.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.060
In fact, we can plot some of the points.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.740
At x is equal to one,

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.870
P of x is also equal to one,

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:14.990
so that point is on the line.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.480
The same thing happens
at x is equal to three.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.620
In between that x is equal to two,

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.740
the value of P of x is four.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.040
So it will be somewhere up here.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.610
And since we know it's a
fourth degree polynomial

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:31.360
or a quartic, we know it'll
be a wibbly wobbly shape.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:34.680
But because it can't pass down
into this region down here,

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.843
it must look something like this.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:43.390
And our question wants
us to find the value

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.130
when x is equal to four.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.400
So when it's somewhere up here,

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.620
finding the value of this polynomial

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.840
at any x value would be easy

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.587
if only we had the equation of this line.

00:09:54.587 --> 00:09:56.210
But the equation of this line

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:57.880
is slightly hard to find

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:00.180
when we look at it on this perspective.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:02.840
Instead, let's take a
look at our inequality.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:05.440
If we subtract x from both sides,

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:07.780
we have that P of x minus x

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:10.010
is bigger than or equal to zero.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.540
Subtracting x off this function

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.030
makes it something that's
easier to find an equation for

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:18.990
because it will intersect the x-axis.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:20.900
Plotting P of x minus x,

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.267
we get something that
looks more like this.

00:10:23.267 --> 00:10:26.090
And you can see where I've
got these points from.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.890
I just subtracted x
from these values here.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:31.890
One minus one would give
us a value of zero there.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:35.260
Four minus two gives
the coordinate two, two

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:39.420
and three minus three gives
the coordinate three, zero.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.800
I know the x-intercepts of this quartic,

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:44.810
so I can actually write its equation.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.670
I'd get K, which is some scale factor

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.380
that we're yet to find.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.140
X minus one squared

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:53.340
times x minus three squared.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.700
If you're slightly
unfamiliar with quartics,

00:10:55.700 --> 00:11:00.130
you may wonder how I know
that these are both squared.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.090
Well, I can tell what
they call the multiplicity

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:06.540
of the zeros by actually
looking at the graph.

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:09.330
Also called the order, the multiplicity

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.470
is how many zeros are at the x-intercept.

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:15.320
For example, if the multiplicity was one,

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.930
that would be if this
bracket wasn't squared.

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:20.620
It was just a single value of x.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.060
In that case, the x-intercept

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:24.770
would be cut in a linear fashion.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:27.700
The intercept would
look something like this

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.120
or like this.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.160
With a multiplicity of two,

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.660
that's when we would see an x squared

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.300
and the intercept would
look like a quadratic,

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.910
something like this or this.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:41.227
This is for a multiplicity of two

00:11:41.227 --> 00:11:44.980
but also four, six, eight

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:47.040
and in fact any even number.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.640
And a multiplicity of three

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:52.680
or of five, seven, nine

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.600
and any other odd number,

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:57.620
we would see something
that looks like this

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.940
where the intercept is in there.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:03.490
Fun fact is the higher this
number of multiplicity,

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.030
the flatter this section will look.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:08.920
Our x-intercepts come down and turn around

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:11.040
in that sort of quadratic function,

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:14.080
so that's why we can say
that that would be squared.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.760
If we're dealing with a quartic,

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.203
that is a power of x to the four,

00:12:18.203 --> 00:12:21.020
then the total
multiplicities added together

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:22.580
will equal four.

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.670
We do still want to find the value of K

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:27.310
and we can do that
using these points here.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:28.840
If we used x equals one,

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.380
we'd end up with one minus one is zero.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:32.460
That would all be zero

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.970
and it wouldn't be useful for finding K.

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:37.430
Same thing would happen if we used three.

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:40.580
That's probably why they've
given us this one in between.

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:44.921
If P of two minus two is equal to two,

00:12:44.921 --> 00:12:49.921
we'd have K, two minus one is one squared,

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:54.580
two minus three is -1 squared.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.950
That would all be one

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:59.150
and K would just be equal to two.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:01.440
So this would be our final equation

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.730
for P of x minus x

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:04.990
and that's all we need

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:07.690
to be able to find P of four.

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:09.790
Plugging in x is equal to four,

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:13.380
it works out to give us the answer of 22.

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:15.410
Luckily, that's one of our options

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:18.460
and so we can say that
B is the right answer.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:19.840
I know that in the real exam,

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.350
you get a lot less time
than I've taken here

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:24.820
but I'm trying to explain things as I go,

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:28.410
especially if this problem is
an unfamiliar type for you.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.070
What makes the exam even harder

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.840
is that this might be
an unfamiliar question

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:34.320
to almost everyone.

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:37.010
It doesn't look like it
appears in last year's exam

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.080
and so there's not really any warning

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.810
to prepare for something like this.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:45.250
Interestingly, this exam made
the news in Turkey this week

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:48.380
after a decision from the
Council of Higher Education

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:51.160
to change the minimum passing score.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.009
Whilst entry to the top universities

00:13:53.009 --> 00:13:55.400
will remain very competitive,

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:59.310
students could still be placed
in a less competitive program

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:02.860
after getting as little
as one question correct.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:06.130
In Turkey, there are many
higher education institutes

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.990
but they're not all of the same quality.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:10.890
Perhaps this decision could lead

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.360
to more low-quality institutes

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.440
offering degrees that don't help

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.960
to reduce the country's unemployment

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:22.060
or we'll see private
universities now accepting anyone

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.810
who's willing to pay the tuition fee.

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:26.050
Thanks for watching this video

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.020
and again, let me know your
thoughts down in the comments.

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:30.340
This video is in honor

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:33.540
of today's Patron Cat of the Day, Latte

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.226
sent in by Connor.

00:14:35.226 --> 00:14:37.976
(tranquil music)

